    {
        "content": "<p>rvolosatovs assigned rvolosatovs to <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14656\">PR #14656</a>.</p>",
        "id": 631036989,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791818593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> rvolosatovs submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14656#pullrequestreview-5492506813\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks, I think this looks good overall, but there are some improvements we could make. I don't think we can avoid having to report the \"real\" error in both places, therefore I think we need to wrap the error in an <code>Arc</code></p>\n<p>I noticed that <code>http_error_code</code> reporting is currently broken on p2, I opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14667\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14667</a>, which also refactors the <code>error_to_p2</code> to take a reference, which we'd need here to use the <code>Arc</code></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631047187,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791820935
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14656#discussion_r4249430938\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is now redundant, right?</p>\n</blockquote>",
