    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14656#discussion_r4249903065\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"suggestion\"><pre><span></span><code>                };\n                let e = Arc::new(e);\n                if let Some(tx) = tx {\n                    let _ = tx.send(StreamEnd::Error(Arc::clone(&amp;e)));\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631047199,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791820936
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14656#discussion_r4249966591\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"suggestion\"><pre><span></span><code>                            match stream.blocking_read(4096) {\n                                Ok(buf) if buf.is_empty() =&gt; break format!(\"eof bytes={bytes}\"),\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is not correct usage according to the spec, since an empty buffer could mean that there are no bytes available at the time. <code>blocking_read</code> should never return an empty buffer</p>\n</blockquote>",
